<BaseLayout title="The Truth About Trans" description="People come before the argument."><article class="prose"><header class="page-hero"><a href="/advocacy/">← Advocacy</a><p class="eyebrow" style="margin-top:18px">Starter draft · awaiting Beth’s personal edit</p><h1>The Truth About Trans</h1><p class="intro">People come before the argument.</p></header><p>The truth about trans people begins with a simple courtesy: we are talking about people. Neighbors, coworkers, friends, and family deserve dignity without having to win a debate first.</p><p>Use the name someone asks you to use. Respect their privacy. Ask sincere questions with care, and accept that nobody is required to turn their life into a public lesson.</p><p>You do not need to understand every part of another person’s experience to treat them well. This space starts there: less spectacle, more listening, and room for people to speak for themselves.</p></article></BaseLayout>
